# Binary / LFS
*.docx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pbix filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Line endings for .NET source (added 2026-08-19)
#
# .editorconfig scopes `end_of_line = crlf` to [*.{cs,csx,vb,vbx}]. Without a
# matching checkout rule the two platforms disagree:
#   - Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks out CRLF  -> `dotnet format` passes locally
#   - Linux CI checks out the stored bytes (LF)     -> `dotnet format` errors on EVERY
#     line break ("Replace 13 characters with '\r\n...'"), so the Format check was
#     permanently red while nothing looked wrong on a developer machine.
#
# These rules force CRLF in the working tree on ALL platforms so local and CI agree
# with .editorconfig. Storage in the repo remains normalized to LF, so this adds no
# content churn and no diff for existing Windows worktrees.
#
# Scope deliberately matches .editorconfig — do NOT broaden to `* text=auto`, which
# would also rewrite shell scripts that must stay LF.
*.cs   text eol=crlf
*.csx  text eol=crlf
*.vb   text eol=crlf
*.vbx  text eol=crlf
